WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.440
The school Week Four practical links catastrophic bleeding, the CAT tourniquet, pelvic binding, fractures, spinal protection and chest injury. Treat these as connected decisions about one changing patient.
学校第4周实训把灾难性出血、CAT止血带、骨盆带、骨折、脊柱保护及胸伤联系在一起。应把它们看成对同一变化患者的一组连续决策。

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:26.016
This lecture follows an original industrial injury, then uses a separate pelvic example. You will explain not only what device you choose, but what problem it should change and how you will detect failure.
本课沿着一个原创工业损伤案例，再加入独立骨盆例子。你不仅要说选什么器械，还要说明它应改变什么问题，以及如何识别失败。

00:00:26.016 --> 00:00:38.664
Nancy supplies the mechanism and assessment reading. The saved school outline supplies the practice targets; the provincial examination snapshot and current service procedures are separately identified.
Nancy提供机制及评估阅读；学校存档大纲提供训练目标；省级考试指南快照与当前服务操作流程会另外标明。

00:00:38.664 --> 00:00:50.232
Reading and narrated rehearsal prepare you for supervised stations. They do not replace the school practical checkoff, actual device instruction or the authorization required for patient care.
阅读及配音演练是监督训练站的准备，不能替代学校实操签核、真实器械说明或患者照护所需授权。

00:00:50.232 --> 00:01:05.520
A forty-one-year-old worker has a thigh trapped by machinery. Qualified rescuers have isolated the machine. There is continuing heavy bleeding from the exposed limb and the patient is anxious, cool and breathing rapidly.
一名41岁工人大腿被机械压住，专业救援人员已经隔离机械。暴露肢体仍大量出血，患者焦虑、皮肤凉且呼吸快。

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:17.664
The pulse is one hundred twenty-two, pressure one hundred six over seventy-four, respiratory rate twenty-eight and saturation ninety-seven percent. The patient can answer questions.
脉搏每分钟122次，血压106/74，呼吸每分钟28次，血氧饱和度97%。患者还能回答问题。

00:01:17.664 --> 00:01:29.208
Talking and a preserved systolic pressure do not exclude serious blood loss. The continuing bleed requires immediate control while the crew checks the other primary threats.
能说话及收缩压尚可，并不能排除严重失血。持续出血需要立即控制，同时团队检查其他初级威胁。

00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:42.024
Do not order an unplanned lift simply because access is difficult. Coordinate clinical preparation with the rescue lead and request the resources needed for a safe release and rapid onward care.
不能因为接近困难，就要求未经计划直接抬开机械。应与救援负责人协调临床准备，并请求安全解除挤压及迅速后送所需资源。

00:01:42.024 --> 00:01:53.880
Mechanism describes how energy reached the patient. Compression can damage muscle and vessels locally, while a fall or secondary impact can create a different injury elsewhere.
损伤机制描述能量如何作用于患者。挤压可在局部损伤肌肉及血管，而跌倒或二次撞击又可在别处造成不同损伤。

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:07.536
Ask what was trapped, how much tissue was involved, how long the compression lasted and what happened before and after the event. Obtain rescue information without allowing a long history to postpone bleeding control.
应询问压住什么、涉及多少组织、持续多久，以及事件前后发生什么。取得救援信息时，不能因长时间问病史而延误止血。

00:02:07.536 --> 00:02:20.568
The visible thigh injury does not clear the chest, abdomen or pelvis. Make a rapid deliberate search for other significant injuries and expand the examination as the situation permits.
可见大腿伤并不代表胸、腹及骨盆没有问题。应快速而有目的地寻找其他重要损伤，并在条件允许时扩大检查。

00:02:20.568 --> 00:02:34.344
A mechanism raises or lowers suspicion; clinical findings and their trend determine the response. Do not diagnose every predicted injury as present or dismiss a concerning finding after a low-speed event.
机制会提高或降低警觉，但反应应依据临床发现及趋势。不能把所有预测损伤都当成已经存在，也不能因低速事件而忽视危险发现。

00:02:34.344 --> 00:02:49.824
MARCH begins with massive hemorrhage, followed by airway, respirations, circulation and hypothermia or head-injury protection. In this case, exsanguinating limb bleeding cannot wait for a lengthy sequential survey.
MARCH先处理大量出血，再处理气道、呼吸、循环，以及低体温预防或头伤保护。本例可能致命的肢体失血，不能等冗长顺序评估完成。

00:02:49.824 --> 00:03:03.408
The current major-trauma guideline calls its sequence C A B C D E, with catastrophic hemorrhage first. The common purpose is rapid correction of reversible threats, not a competition between mnemonics.
当前严重创伤指南使用以灾难性出血开头的CABCDE顺序。共同目的都是迅速纠正可逆威胁，不是比较哪套口诀更好。

00:03:03.408 --> 00:03:16.848
This does not mean every minor traumatic wound outranks an obstructed airway. Judge the actual threat; when personnel are available, hemorrhage control and airway or breathing support proceed in parallel.
这不代表每个轻微创伤伤口都比气道阻塞优先。应判断真实威胁；有人手时，止血与气道或呼吸支持应并行。

00:03:16.848 --> 00:03:28.728
After any intervention or patient change, return to the primary survey. A mnemonic helps organize attention but cannot prove that every threat has been found or corrected.
每次干预或患者变化后，都应回到初级评估。口诀可组织注意力，却不能证明所有威胁都已找到或纠正。

00:03:28.728 --> 00:03:39.312
Assign one clinician to the visible bleed and another to airway, breathing and the wider patient assessment. State tasks aloud and confirm they are understood.
应安排一位临床人员处理可见出血，另一位负责气道、呼吸及更广泛患者评估。任务应说清，并确认对方理解。

00:03:39.312 --> 00:03:50.592
Agree with the rescue lead how access and release will occur. Rescue isolation is not a one-time assumption; new movement or equipment can create another hazard.
应与救援负责人商定接近及解除挤压方式。机械隔离不能只作一次假设；新的移动或器械可能产生新危险。

00:03:50.592 --> 00:04:01.440
Call out whether the bleeding has actually stopped, not merely that the tourniquet is on. Tell the team immediately about worsening mentation, breathing or perfusion.
应通报出血是否真实停止，而不只是说止血带已上。意识、呼吸或灌注变差时，应立即告诉团队。

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:14.160
Maintain a transfer plan while procedures occur. A difficult vein or an attractive training task must not make the crew lose awareness of time, ongoing loss or the need for definitive control.
操作过程中仍应维持转运方案。困难静脉或有吸引力的训练项目，不能让团队忽略时间、持续失血或确定性止血需要。

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:25.464
Saturation describes the proportion of measured hemoglobin binding sites carrying oxygen. It does not measure the amount of hemoglobin remaining or the flow reaching the tissues.
血氧饱和度描述被测血红蛋白结合位点携氧的比例，不测量剩余血红蛋白总量，也不测量到达组织的血流。

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:40.296
With hemorrhage, sympathetic compensation may preserve cuff pressure while peripheral perfusion deteriorates. A rapid weak pulse, cool skin, tachypnea or changing behavior may be important before hypotension.
失血时，交感代偿可能维持袖带血压，但外周灌注已经恶化。低血压之前，快而弱的脉搏、皮肤凉、呼吸快或行为变化，都可能重要。

00:04:40.296 --> 00:04:53.736
Use the whole pattern and repeated measurements. Medicines, age, pain, temperature and spinal injury can alter the expected signs, so no single absent feature safely excludes shock.
应看整体模式及反复测量。药物、年龄、疼痛、温度及脊髓损伤都可改变预期征象，因此缺少一个特征不能安全排除休克。

00:04:53.736 --> 00:05:06.264
Do not stand or sit an unstable injured patient up to prove hypovolemia. You already have a clinical problem requiring treatment and reassessment without a provocative orthostatic test.
不能让不稳定伤者站起或坐起，只为证明低血容量。现有临床问题已经需要处理及复评，不必再做可能诱发恶化的体位性试验。

00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:20.520
A successful dressing or tourniquet controls one source, not the entire circulation. Major loss can remain concealed in the chest, abdomen, retroperitoneum, pelvis or injured soft tissues.
成功敷料或止血带控制的是一个来源，而不是整个循环。重要失血仍可能隐藏在胸、腹、腹膜后、骨盆或受伤软组织。

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:32.016
Expose and examine purposefully, including the back when it can be accessed safely. Do not repeatedly roll an unstable patient simply to finish a routine checklist.
应有目的地暴露及检查，安全可及的背部也应考虑。不能只为完成常规清单，就反复翻滚不稳定患者。

00:05:32.016 --> 00:05:45.336
Look for tenderness, deformity, wounds, asymmetric breathing and evolving perfusion. Early absence of bruising or a normal initial pressure is not a dependable internal-bleeding rule-out.
应检查压痛、畸形、伤口、呼吸不对称及变化中的灌注。早期没有瘀青或初次血压正常，不能可靠排除内出血。

00:05:45.336 --> 00:05:58.512
If bleeding cannot be definitively controlled in the field, minimize delay and move toward the appropriate trauma resource. A second bag of clear fluid cannot substitute for stopping an internal bleed.
若院前无法确定性止血，应减少延误并转向适当创伤资源。再加一袋透明液体，不能替代停止内出血。

00:05:58.512 --> 00:06:09.744
Use appropriate protection and expose the relevant area enough to identify the source. Do not spend time naming the vessel before acting on an obvious life-threatening bleed.
应采用适当防护，并充分暴露相关部位找到来源。明显危及生命的出血，不能先花时间确认血管名称再行动。

00:06:09.744 --> 00:06:20.304
Apply firm direct pressure at the wound. A dressing is useful only when it helps deliver effective pressure; loosely covering the blood is not source control.
应在伤口直接施加有力压迫。敷料只有帮助形成有效压力才有用；松松盖住血液并不是控制出血源。

00:06:20.304 --> 00:06:32.592
Assess whether the bleeding stops. For severe extremity bleeding that is not controlled promptly, prepare the indicated tourniquet instead of repeatedly restarting ineffective pressure attempts.
应判断出血是否停止。严重肢体出血未能及时控制时，应准备有指征的止血带，而不是反复重启无效直接压迫。

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:46.104
If pressure succeeds, maintain control and secure an appropriate dressing while continuing the primary survey. Recheck after movement and do not assume a neat exterior excludes bleeding beneath it.
压迫成功后，应维持控制并妥善固定敷料，同时继续初级评估。搬运后要复查，不能以外面整齐就假定下面没有出血。

00:06:46.104 --> 00:06:59.040
The tool must fit the anatomy. A limb tourniquet can compress an arm or leg circumferentially, but cannot be placed around the chest, abdomen or neck as an ordinary bleeding treatment.
工具必须适合解剖。肢体止血带可环绕上肢或下肢压迫，却不能把胸、腹或颈部当作普通止血部位来环绕。

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:10.488
Eligible penetrating junctional wounds may benefit from packing when direct pressure alone is inadequate. The reviewed local procedure excludes neck, chest and abdominal packing.
直接压迫不足时，适合的穿透性交界伤口可能受益于填塞。已核查当地流程排除了颈部、胸部及腹部填塞。

00:07:10.488 --> 00:07:23.016
Internal bleeding requires a different plan: control what is accessible, stabilize relevant injuries, preserve temperature and perfusion, and arrange rapid appropriate definitive care.
内出血需要不同方案：控制可处理来源、稳定相关损伤、保护温度及灌注，并安排迅速送往适当确定性照护。

00:07:23.016 --> 00:07:36.912
A visibly unsuccessful intervention requires reassessment, not merely repetition of its name. State the failed endpoint and choose the next indicated action while maintaining any control already achieved.
干预明显失败时，应复评，而不是只重复操作名称。应说明哪个终点未达到，选择下一项有指征行动，同时保留已取得的控制。

00:07:36.912 --> 00:07:47.544
For the reviewed local limb procedure, place the tourniquet five to eight centimetres proximal to the injury, or as high on the limb as needed, and not over a joint.
按已核查当地肢体流程，止血带位于伤口近心端五至八厘米，或按需要置于尽可能高的肢体位置，不能放在关节上。

00:07:47.544 --> 00:08:04.008
Current PR03 specifies direct skin contact. Do not introduce generic padding or place the device over a solid object in clothing; a source-specific emergency over-clothing instruction is not a universal deliberate-placement rule.
当前PR03要求直接接触皮肤。不能擅加泛用垫料，也不能压在衣内硬物上；特定来源的紧急隔衣指示，不是所有有条件定位操作的通用规则。

00:08:04.008 --> 00:08:16.416
The reviewed example is CAT Generation Seven with a single routing buckle. Confirm the actual device at the school station rather than importing another generation or improvised belt technique.
本课已核查示例是单路径扣的CAT第七代。应在学校训练站确认真实器械，不能搬用其他代际或临时皮带技术。

00:08:16.416 --> 00:08:29.736
Keep source control active while exposing and preparing. If the scene prevents deliberate placement, follow the applicable emergency procedure and communicate exactly what was applied and where.
暴露及准备时仍要维持止血。若现场条件不允许常规有条件定位，应依适用紧急流程处理，并准确交代用了什么、放在哪里。

00:08:29.736 --> 00:08:41.688
On the reviewed Gen Seven device, route the band through its single buckle path and pull the band firmly back onto itself. Excess slack reduces effective circumferential compression.
对已核查第七代器械，应把带身穿过单一路径扣，再牢固回贴。带身松弛会降低有效环周压迫。

00:08:41.688 --> 00:08:50.376
Tighten the windlass to stop the bleeding, then secure it in the clip and retain the rod and band with the time strap according to the device instructions.
应收紧绞棒直到止血，再按器械说明锁入固定卡，并用时间带固定绞棒及带身。

00:08:50.376 --> 00:09:03.528
Do not stop after a memorized number of turns. Limb size, slack and application quality vary; the clinically relevant endpoint is control, not the appearance of having completed the motions.
不能转到背熟的圈数就停。肢体粗细、松弛程度及应用质量各异；临床相关终点是控制出血，不是看起来已走完动作。

00:09:03.528 --> 00:09:15.720
Practice on the instructor-approved trainer and limb model. Do not repeatedly fully occlude an uninjured classmate or reuse a clinical single-use device as though a practice reset renewed it.
应在教师批准的训练器械及肢体模型上练习。不能反复完全阻断未受伤同学的血流，也不能把临床一次性器械重置后当作已恢复新品。

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:27.912
Look at the wound after locking the device. The reviewed CAT instructions also require a distal pulse check: continuing bleeding or a persisting distal pulse means reassessment of effectiveness.
锁定器械后应看伤口。已核查CAT说明也要求检查远端脉搏：若仍出血或远端仍有脉搏，就需重新判断效果。

00:09:27.912 --> 00:09:39.960
Further tightening or an additional device immediately proximal and beside the first may be needed under the applicable instruction. Do not place a second device distal to the bleeding source.
按适用说明，可能需要继续收紧，或在第一条近心端紧邻再加一条。不能把第二条放在出血源远心端。

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:54.000
An effective tourniquet intentionally sacrifices distal arterial flow to control life-threatening loss. This differs from a routine splint circulation check and does not justify periodically letting blood through.
有效止血带会有意阻断远端动脉流，以控制致命失血。它不同于普通夹板的循环检查，因此不能定期松开让血流通过。

00:09:54.000 --> 00:10:09.072
Keep it visible, record the application time and provide indicated analgesia without releasing control. If prolonged scene or conveyance time approaches the guideline concern, consult rather than automatically removing it.
应保持可见、记录时间，并在不松开止血的前提下提供有指征镇痛。若现场或转运时间接近指南关注范围，应咨询，不能自动拆除。

00:10:09.072 --> 00:10:21.000
The Week Four outline specifies a sixty-second CAT performance target. Rehearse an efficient sequence on the school trainer instead of slowing down to narrate a long essay during application.
第4周大纲规定CAT六十秒表现目标。应在学校训练器械上练习高效顺序，不能应用时为讲一大段说明而拖慢。

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:32.424
Speed without correct position, effective compression and secure locking is not useful. Record the time and report the observed bleeding endpoint as distinct facts.
若没有正确位置、有效压迫及牢固锁定，速度就没有意义。记录应用时间时，应把时间与观察到的止血终点作为不同事实。

00:10:32.424 --> 00:10:45.672
The saved Week Four outline does not fully define the starting device configuration or every clock boundary. Obtain that actual station instruction rather than claiming an invented official pass rubric.
第4周存档大纲没有完整定义器械起始状态及所有计时边界。应取得真实训练站指示，不能把自编标准称作官方通过评分表。

00:10:45.672 --> 00:10:59.568
On a real patient, do not wait for sixty seconds to act or stop correcting an ineffective device because the practice clock ended. Urgency, effective control and reassessment remain the clinical priorities.
对真实患者，不能等六十秒才行动，也不能因为训练计时结束就停止纠正无效器械。临床优先仍是及时、有效止血及复评。

00:10:59.568 --> 00:11:12.216
For an eligible deep wound, packing transfers pressure toward the bleeding source rather than merely absorbing blood at the skin opening. Use the actual gauze or hemostatic product and trained method.
对适合的深伤口，填塞是把压力传向出血源，而不是只在皮肤入口吸血。应采用真实纱布或止血产品及已受训练的方法。

00:11:12.216 --> 00:11:23.184
The reviewed local procedure maintains pressure during tight packing, then applies very firm direct pressure for at least three minutes before securement and ongoing reassessment.
已核查当地流程要求紧密填塞时维持压力，然后至少三分钟持续有力直接压迫，再固定并持续复评。

00:11:23.184 --> 00:11:37.248
Do not import the textbook suggestion of a guaranteed two-minute hemostatic effect. Material, wound, medication and application quality differ, and ongoing bleeding means the endpoint has not been reached.
不能照搬教材中保证两分钟产生止血效果的说法。材料、伤口、药物及应用质量不同；仍在出血就代表终点未达到。

00:11:37.248 --> 00:11:52.392
Neck, chest and abdomen are excluded by the reviewed PR04. A wound that cannot be packed safely needs its appropriate alternative strategy and rapid definitive care, not improvised insertion into a body cavity.
已核查PR04排除了颈、胸及腹部。不能安全填塞的伤口，需要适当替代方案及迅速确定性照护，不是临时向体腔内塞东西。

00:11:52.392 --> 00:12:01.080
Before the rescue lift or stretcher movement, check that dressings and tourniquets are secure and that the team knows which injury needs protection.
救援抬举或担架移动前，应确认敷料及止血带牢固，并让团队知道哪处损伤需要保护。

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:13.152
After movement, look again for renewed bleeding and device displacement. A higher blood pressure can also reveal an inadequate application that seemed to work during profound shock.
移动后应再次寻找重新出血及器械移位。血压升高后，原先在严重休克时似乎有效的不足应用，也可能暴露出来。

00:12:13.152 --> 00:12:24.120
Reassess the patient beyond the wound. A continuing rapid weak pulse or worsening breathing requires a broader explanation than the statement that the bandage looks dry.
复评不能只看伤口。若仍快而弱的脉搏，或呼吸恶化，就需要比“绷带看着干”更广泛的解释。

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:35.328
Call out any recurrence, the correction and its effect. Document a change honestly instead of rewriting the record to make control appear uninterrupted.
任何复发、纠正及效果都应通报。应如实记录变化，不能修改叙述，让止血看起来从未中断。

00:12:35.328 --> 00:12:48.120
In a separate original example, a fifty-seven-year-old has pelvic pain after a side-impact collision. The pulse is one hundred sixteen and pressure eighty-eight over fifty-six, with cool skin.
另一个原创例子中，一名57岁患者侧面撞车后骨盆痛，脉搏每分钟116次，血压88/56，皮肤凉。

00:12:48.120 --> 00:13:01.992
The mechanism and perfusion findings raise concern for significant pelvic injury and concealed bleeding. Absence of an obvious open wound or dramatic abdominal distension does not make the patient stable.
机制及灌注发现提示重要骨盆损伤及隐匿失血。没有明显开放伤口或显著腹胀，并不代表患者稳定。

00:13:01.992 --> 00:13:14.016
Assess gently and do not repeatedly rock the pelvis to prove instability. Search for associated injuries and prepare early indicated binding with a coordinated movement plan.
应轻柔评估，不能反复摇晃骨盆证明不稳。应寻找伴随损伤，及早准备有指征绑带，并协调搬运。

00:13:14.016 --> 00:13:27.936
A binder is part of source-directed hemorrhage control and urgent conveyance, not a definitive diagnosis. Continue airway, breathing and circulation reassessment while arranging the appropriate trauma destination.
骨盆带是针对出血源控制及紧急转运的一部分，不是确定诊断。安排适当创伤目的地时，仍应继续气道、呼吸及循环复评。

00:13:27.936 --> 00:13:42.960
Use the actual indication rather than binding every painful hip. The reviewed criteria combine a major mechanism with findings such as instability of perfusion, pelvic pain, reduced consciousness or a distracting major injury.
应使用真实指征，不能给每个髋痛患者都绑带。已核查标准把重大机制与灌注不稳、骨盆痛、意识降低或分散注意的重要损伤等发现结合。

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:52.992
Palpate the greater-trochanter level and centre the binder there. A belt placed around the waist or over the iliac crests is too high for the intended compression.
应定位股骨大转子水平，并把骨盆带中心放在那里。环腰或髂嵴水平的带子，对预期压迫来说太高。

00:13:52.992 --> 00:14:06.744
An isolated neck-of-femur fracture and simple standing-height fall are exclusions in the reviewed local procedure. An older adult with a shortened rotated leg is not automatically an unstable pelvic-ring case.
已核查当地流程排除了单纯股骨颈骨折及简单站立高度跌倒。长者下肢缩短外旋，并不自动代表不稳定骨盆环损伤。

00:14:06.744 --> 00:14:19.752
Follow the real binder model for sizing, closure and tension. Do not turn the T-POD cutting instructions or a textbook folded-sheet method into a universal procedure for every commercial product.
尺码、闭合及张力应按真实骨盆带型号。不能把T-POD剪裁指示或教材折单方法，当成所有商业产品通用程序。

00:14:19.752 --> 00:14:32.760
Plan application and transfer to avoid unnecessary rolling of a suspected unstable pelvis. The movement leader coordinates the crew and explains the plan to the patient when possible.
应规划应用及转移，避免无必要翻滚疑似不稳骨盆。搬运负责人协调团队，条件允许时向患者解释。

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:44.448
After each movement, check binder position and tension and repeat the broader patient assessment. Improvement in one pressure reading does not exclude continued bleeding elsewhere.
每次移动后，都应检查骨盆带位置及张力，并重复更广泛患者评估。一次血压改善，并不能排除别处仍在失血。

00:14:44.448 --> 00:14:56.784
Do not routinely loosen a working binder for another stability examination. If it becomes displaced or is accidentally released, address the problem and communicate the actual sequence.
不能为了再做一次稳定性检查，就常规松开有效骨盆带。若移位或意外松脱，应处理问题，并如实沟通过程。

00:14:56.784 --> 00:15:09.408
Record application time, the indication, findings before and after, and any device problem. The receiving team needs a defensible clinical story, not just the phrase pelvis bound.
应记录应用时间、指征、前后发现及器械问题。接收团队需要有依据的临床过程，不只是“骨盆已绑”一句话。

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:22.752
Assess distal circulation, sensation and motor function before stabilization when it does not delay life-saving control. Compare relevant findings with the opposite limb and record limitations.
在不延误救命控制时，稳定前应评估远端循环、感觉及运动。相关发现可与对侧比较，并记录检查受限原因。

00:15:22.752 --> 00:15:33.912
Support the injury, provide indicated analgesia and choose the appropriate splint. Do not force movement through an injured joint merely to complete a motor checklist.
应支持损伤、提供有指征镇痛并选择适当夹板。不能只为完成运动清单，就强迫受伤关节活动。

00:15:33.912 --> 00:15:49.176
The assigned provincial guide allows limited realignment in selected gross deformity or distal pulselessness circumstances. That is not unrestricted fracture reduction; use the actual taught procedure and stop if the plan is unsafe.
指定省级指南在某些严重畸形或远端无脉情况下允许有限度重新对线。这不是无限制骨折复位；应按真实受教流程，方案不安全时停止。

00:15:49.176 --> 00:16:03.576
Recheck after splinting and movement. New pain, numbness, weakness or impaired perfusion can indicate a device or injury problem requiring prompt reassessment, not a normal price of immobilization.
夹板后及搬运后要复查。新发疼痛、麻木、无力或灌注受损，可能提示器械或损伤问题，需要及时复评，不能当成固定的正常代价。

00:16:03.576 --> 00:16:14.640
If an extremity part is separated, manage the patient first. Do not let a search for the part postpone airway support, life-threatening bleeding control or urgent departure.
若肢体部分离断，应先处理患者。寻找离断部分，不能延误气道支持、致命出血控制或紧急出发。

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:25.032
The assigned guide describes gentle removal of gross contamination, saline-moistened sterile gauze, a protective bag and cool protected storage with the patient.
指定指南描述轻柔去除明显污染，以盐水湿润无菌纱布、保护袋及低温保护方式保存，并随患者转运。

00:16:25.032 --> 00:16:36.768
Do not place tissue directly on ice, immerse it in water, use dry ice or warm it. Protect the part from additional damage and keep its identity linked to the correct patient.
不能把组织直接放冰上、浸水、使用干冰或加热。应避免进一步损害，并保持与正确患者身份对应。

00:16:36.768 --> 00:16:48.744
Communicate what was recovered and how it was handled. Replantation suitability is determined by the receiving specialists, not guaranteed by a particular appearance or transport promise.
应沟通找到哪些部分及如何处理。能否再植由接收专科判断，不是凭某种外观或转运承诺就能保证。

00:16:48.744 --> 00:17:01.368
A crush injury is local tissue damage from compression. Crush syndrome is a systemic problem that can follow substantial muscle injury and release; not every briefly trapped finger develops it.
挤压伤是压迫造成的局部组织损伤。挤压综合征是在大量肌肉损伤及解除压迫后可能出现的全身问题，不是每个短暂夹住的手指都会发生。

00:17:01.368 --> 00:17:13.368
Damaged muscle can release potassium and other cellular contents when circulation returns. Fluid shifts and metabolic disturbance can worsen perfusion and trigger dangerous dysrhythmias.
血流恢复时，受损肌肉可释放钾及其他细胞内容物。液体转移及代谢紊乱可加重灌注问题，并引发危险心律失常。

00:17:13.368 --> 00:17:24.840
Muscle breakdown also creates risk for later kidney injury. Dark urine may be a clue when present, but it is not necessary before the team prepares for a dangerous release.
肌肉分解也造成后续肾损伤风险。出现深色尿时可作为线索，但团队不能等它出现才为危险解除挤压做准备。

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:36.552
Degree of force, muscle mass, duration and associated injury influence risk. Do not convert a single entrapment-time number into a universal safe-release guarantee.
力量大小、肌肉量、持续时间及伴随损伤共同影响风险。不能把某个受困时间数字，变成普遍安全解除的保证。

00:17:36.552 --> 00:17:49.680
Coordinate the lift with the rescue lead and the clinical team. Request advanced resources early when indicated, and prepare for sudden deterioration rather than treating release as the end of the problem.
应与救援负责人及临床团队协调抬举。有指征时及早请求高级资源，并准备突然恶化，不能把解除挤压当成问题结束。

00:17:49.680 --> 00:18:03.672
The current crush guideline recommends consultation for the pre-release fluid and tourniquet plan. A tourniquet for an uncontrolled bleed and a considered pre-release crush strategy are related but distinct indications.
当前挤压指南建议就解除前液体及止血带方案进行咨询。控制未止肢体出血，与考虑中的解除前挤压策略，是有关但不同的指征。

00:18:03.672 --> 00:18:18.312
Salbutamol for the crush-related electrolyte concern requires CliniCall consultation in that guideline. Do not give the drug just because it is carried, or import advanced electrolyte treatment into independent PCP practice.
该指南中，针对挤压相关电解质问题使用沙丁胺醇，需要CliniCall咨询。不能因为车上有药就给，也不能把高级电解质治疗搬成独立PCP操作。

00:18:18.312 --> 00:18:32.784
After release, repeat airway, breathing, circulation and rhythm assessment and move toward appropriate definitive care. A normal initial tracing does not guarantee that the subsequent course will remain normal.
解除后，应重复气道、呼吸、循环及心律评估，并推进适当确定性照护。最初心电图正常，不保证后续仍正常。

00:18:32.784 --> 00:18:45.264
For uncontrolled hemorrhage, clear crystalloid does not replace oxygen-carrying red cells or definitive hemostasis. Excess fluid can dilute coagulation and worsen the situation.
对未控制失血，透明晶体液不能替代携氧红细胞或确定性止血。过多液体可能稀释凝血并使情况更差。

00:18:45.264 --> 00:18:59.712
Selected major-trauma pathways use limited crystalloid and permissive hypotension while maintaining critical perfusion. This is a specific clinical strategy, not permission to ignore worsening mentation or a falling pressure.
某些严重创伤路径在维持关键灌注的同时，采用限制晶体液及允许性低血压。这是特定临床策略，不是忽视意识恶化或血压下降的许可。

00:18:59.712 --> 00:19:14.952
Suspected brain injury and clear spinal cord deficit create important exceptions to a low-pressure approach. State the applicable pathway and seek clinical support when priorities conflict rather than averaging incompatible targets.
疑似脑伤及明确脊髓神经缺损，是低血压策略的重要例外。应说明适用路径，优先冲突时取得临床支持，不能把不相容目标取平均。

00:19:14.952 --> 00:19:30.168
Assess the indication, delivery and response for each actual fluid increment. New respiratory distress, crackles or worsening perfusion demands reassessment; a planned maximum is not a required volume to finish.
每次真实液体增量，都要检查指征、给入及反应。新呼吸困难、湿啰音或灌注恶化，都需要复评；计划最大量不是必须完成的体积。

00:19:30.168 --> 00:19:41.616
Tranexamic acid reduces fibrin breakdown. It does not mechanically close a vessel, replace lost blood or remove the need for pressure, a binder or definitive care.
氨甲环酸减少纤维蛋白分解。它不能机械闭合血管、补回血液，也不能取代压迫、骨盆带或确定性照护。

00:19:41.616 --> 00:19:54.192
Use the actual trauma criteria, timing, exclusions and authorized route. An impressive wound without the indicated systemic context is not automatically the same as the guideline treatment group.
应使用真实创伤标准、时间条件、排除项及获准途径。外观严重但没有相应全身背景的伤口，不自动等于指南治疗对象。

00:19:54.192 --> 00:20:06.120
The current service monograph and a school calculation label are different sources. Do not convert an exercise answer into an order or use the trauma medicine for gastrointestinal bleeding.
当前服务药物专论与学校计算标签属于不同来源。不能把练习答案变成医嘱，也不能把创伤用药用于胃肠道出血。

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:19.464
When indicated, verify patient, product, dose, route, access and delivery time, then reassess and document. Continue all essential hemorrhage and conveyance actions in parallel.
有指征时，应核对患者、产品、剂量、途径、通路及给入时间，再复评并记录。所有关键止血及转运动作应并行继续。

00:20:19.464 --> 00:20:30.960
A bleeding patient can become cold even on a day that feels comfortable to the crew. Exposure, wet clothing, cold ground and large fluid volumes all matter.
即使团队觉得天气舒服，出血患者仍可能变冷。暴露、湿衣、冷地面及大量液体都重要。

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:42.696
Expose to locate injury, then cover again. Insulation beneath the patient is as important as a blanket on top; use the vehicle and approved warming equipment appropriately.
应为了寻找损伤而暴露，然后重新覆盖。患者身下隔热与上方盖毯同样重要；应适当利用车内环境及批准保暖器械。

00:20:42.696 --> 00:20:55.608
Preventing hypothermia helps protect coagulation, but must not hide a recurrent bleed or obstruct airway access. Arrange warming around the ongoing treatment and observation plan.
预防低体温有助保护凝血，但不能因此遮住复发出血或妨碍气道接近。保暖应围绕持续治疗及观察方案安排。

00:20:55.608 --> 00:21:07.032
A heater is not the treatment for environmental heat stroke, and burn cooling requires simultaneous whole-patient protection. The next lecture separates these different temperature problems.
暖风不是环境性热射病的治疗；烧伤局部降温时，也需同时保护全身。后续课程会区分这些不同温度问题。

00:21:07.032 --> 00:21:19.680
After release and transfer, the original worker becomes more breathless, one side is quieter and pressure falls. The thigh tourniquet remains secure without renewed visible bleeding.
解除及转移后，原工人更气促，一侧呼吸音变弱，血压下降。大腿止血带仍固定，未见再次明显出血。

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:32.688
Do not conclude that every abnormality must be the thigh or crush syndrome. Reassess the primary survey and consider a chest injury, continued concealed loss and other supported explanations.
不能认定所有异常都一定来自大腿或挤压综合征。应重做初级评估，考虑胸伤、持续隐匿失血及其他有依据解释。

00:21:32.688 --> 00:21:46.512
Support oxygenation and ventilation as needed, request the appropriate advanced response and communicate the change. Recognition of a likely advanced procedure need does not grant independent authority to perform it.
应按需要支持氧合及通气，请求适当高级响应，并通报变化。认识到可能需要高级操作，不等于获得独立实施权限。

00:21:46.512 --> 00:21:56.952
State what changed, what should have improved and what got worse. Your handover must include both the successful limb control and the new unresolved threat.
应说清实际变了什么、原应改善什么，以及什么变坏了。交接中既要包含肢体成功止血，也要包含新的未解决威胁。

00:21:56.952 --> 00:22:07.776
The school Saturday includes a five-minute secondary medication-math checkpoint. These are original preparation questions, not the recovered school test or its pass score.
学校周六包括五分钟第二次用药计算检查。这里是原创准备题，不是恢复出的学校试题或通过分数。

00:22:07.776 --> 00:22:20.424
For a simulation-only label of one hundred milligrams per millilitre, one point five grams is fifteen hundred milligrams. Dividing by one hundred milligrams per millilitre gives fifteen millilitres.
对仅用于模拟的每毫升100毫克标签，1.5克等于1500毫克。除以每毫升100毫克，结果为15毫升。

00:22:20.424 --> 00:22:34.008
For two hundred fifty millilitres over forty minutes, the pump rate is three hundred seventy-five millilitres per hour. With fifteen drops per millilitre, the gravity rate is about ninety-four drops per minute.
250毫升用40分钟，泵速为每小时375毫升。若每毫升15滴，重力滴速约为每分钟94滴。

00:22:34.008 --> 00:22:44.952
Write the units and verify the answer against the label and time. No amount, rate or drug implied by this exercise is an instruction to treat the trauma patient.
应写单位，并对照标签及时间核查答案。本题中的量、速度或隐含药物，都不是治疗该创伤患者的指示。

00:22:44.952 --> 00:22:55.560
MIST organizes mechanism, injuries, signs and treatments. Include the relevant event and entrapment timing, not every detail gathered from bystanders.
MIST组织机制、损伤、征象及治疗。应包括相关事件及受困时间，不必把旁观者所有细节都塞进去。

00:22:55.560 --> 00:23:06.672
Describe the important findings and what remains suspected. Keep a clinical concern distinct from a confirmed diagnosis and identify an unexamined region honestly.
应描述重要发现及仍属疑似的问题。临床关注与确定诊断应区分，未检查区域要如实说明。

00:23:06.672 --> 00:23:21.480
Give the trend: initial pressure, later deterioration, effective limb control, application time and the current breathing concern. The receiver needs the direction of travel, not just a single old set of vitals.
应提供趋势：初始血压、后续恶化、有效肢体止血、应用时间，以及当前呼吸问题。接收方需要变化方向，不只是一组过时生命体征。

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:33.696
Finish with what is needed now and confirm transfer of responsibility. MIST is the school rehearsal tool; use any additional operational handover fields required by the receiving service.
最后应说明现在需要什么，并确认责任交接。MIST是学校演练工具；接收服务若另有操作性交接字段，也应完成。

00:23:33.696 --> 00:23:46.536
At the first station, identify the indication and demonstrate the actual CAT sequence on the approved model. Record performance time separately from whether the bleeding-control endpoint was achieved.
第一站应识别指征，并在批准模型上展示真实CAT顺序。表现用时应与是否达到止血终点分别记录。

00:23:46.536 --> 00:23:57.120
At the second station, explain why the pelvis should or should not be bound, identify the greater trochanters and demonstrate the supervised device and movement plan.
第二站应解释为什么应该或不应该使用骨盆带，定位股骨大转子，并展示监督下器械及搬运方案。

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:09.288
At the third station, brief the rescue release and respond to a changing patient. Include an immediate clinical contingency, request for support and concise MIST handover.
第三站应简报救援解除方案，并应对患者变化。内容包括即时临床预案、支援请求及简洁MIST交接。

00:24:09.288 --> 00:24:22.056
Across stations, use closed loop, protect warmth and reassess after intervention or movement. A correct spoken answer does not by itself establish a safe hands-on performance.
各站都应使用闭环、保护温度，并在干预或移动后复评。口头答案正确，本身并不证明实操安全。

00:24:22.056 --> 00:24:36.744
The school links add helpful perspectives on musculoskeletal injury, chest trauma, spinal motion, brain injury, tranexamic acid, hypothermia and older adults. They do not all have the same review depth or authority.
学校链接补充了肌肉骨骼损伤、胸伤、脊柱移动、脑损伤、氨甲环酸、低体温及老年患者的视角。各链接的审阅深度及权威性并不相同。

00:24:36.744 --> 00:24:52.248
Several articles date from 2009 to 2016 and some explain United States practice. Keep their mechanisms and cases separate from any old dose, threshold, device landmark or provider authorization.
多篇文章发表于2009至2016年，部分介绍美国实践。应把机制及案例与旧剂量、阈值、器械定位或人员授权分开。

00:24:52.248 --> 00:25:11.568
Use the current BCEHS pathway and monograph for BC practice. H06 essentials prefer a commercial vented chest seal or leaving an open wound open, while its FR subsection still includes three-sided-dressing wording; confirm the applicable local instruction rather than averaging the two.
卑诗省实践应使用BCEHS现行流程及药物专论。H06要点优先商用通气式胸封或让伤口开放，但FR小节仍包含三边敷料说法；应确认当地适用指示，而不是把两者平均成新规则。

00:25:11.568 --> 00:25:25.584
CRASH-3 provides trial evidence for defined adults and timing. It is not a diagnosis, a universal indication or permission to treat; eligibility remains governed by the current local protocol.
CRASH-3提供特定成人及时间条件下的试验证据。它不是诊断、通用指征或治疗许可；患者是否适用仍由当地现行流程决定。

00:25:25.584 --> 00:26:11.592
Complete the literal pressure definitions before applying the trauma trend. Systolic pressure reflects the arterial peak during ventricular ejection; diastolic pressure remains between beats and is not zero because the ventricle relaxes. Pulse pressure is their difference: a reading of 118 over 76 has a pulse pressure of 42 millimetres of mercury. Stroke volume is volume per beat, not the force required for a beat. Pulse pressure is influenced by ejection, arterial properties and valve disease and does not directly measure stroke volume in millilitres. Do not turn the source adult stroke-volume example into a universal diagnostic interval or infer a blood-loss percentage from one cuff reading.
应用创伤趋势前先完成字面血压定义。收缩压反映心室射血时的动脉峰压；舒张压在两搏之间仍存在，不会因心室舒张就变零。脉压是二者之差：118/76的脉压为42mmHg。每搏量是每搏的体积，不是搏动所需力量。脉压受射血、动脉性质及瓣膜病影响，不能直接量出多少毫升每搏量。不能把来源成人每搏量示例当统一诊断区间，也不能凭一次袖带值推失血百分比。

00:26:11.592 --> 00:27:00.000
The actual assigned factor page names cardiac output, peripheral resistance, circulating volume, viscosity and vessel-wall properties. Cardiac output is heart rate times stroke volume. Resistance relates the pressure difference to flow; compliance describes how readily a vessel expands with added volume or pressure. They are not synonyms, despite the source heading defining resistance as compliance. A narrower vessel can increase resistance, greater viscosity can impede flow, and stiff arteries alter pulsatile pressure. These influences can change together, so an increase in one does not guarantee a fixed final pressure. Compensatory vasoconstriction can preserve a cuff value while hemorrhage and tissue-perfusion failure continue.
实际指定因素页列心排量、外周阻力、循环容量、黏度及血管壁性质。心排量等于心率乘每搏量。阻力联系压差与流量；顺应性描述增加容量或压力时血管容易扩张的程度。二者不是同义词，尽管来源该标题下把阻力定义成顺应性。管腔变窄可增阻，黏度增大可妨碍流动，动脉僵硬会改变脉动压力。多因素可同时变化，一项增加不保证最终血压按固定幅度改变。代偿收缩可维持袖带值，而出血及组织灌注失败仍在持续。

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:46.872
Separate atrial filling responses from the arterial pressure reflex. In the usual arterial baroreflex, rising pressure increases stretch signalling from the carotid-sinus and aortic regions; the response reduces sympathetic drive and increases cardiac vagal influence, tending to lower rate and vascular tone. A fall in pressure tends toward the opposite response. The source paragraph about atrial filling and a faster rate must not be memorized as rising arterial pressure always speeds the heart. Atrial-volume reflexes, illness and medicines add context. Reassess mentation, skin, breathing, pulse and the treated injury rather than declaring successful perfusion from pressure alone.
须区分心房充盈反应与动脉压力反射。通常动脉压力感受器反射中，血压升使颈动脉窦及主动脉区域牵张信号增加，反应为减交感、增心脏迷走影响，倾向降低心率及血管张力；血压下降则倾向相反反应。来源心房充盈及心率增加段，不能背成动脉压升就必心跳加快。心房容量反射、疾病和药物都增加背景因素。须重评意识、皮肤、呼吸、脉搏及已处理损伤，不能只凭血压宣布灌注成功。

00:27:46.872 --> 00:28:37.680
Use the assigned tissue glossary as a structure-to-function map. Histology studies tissue organization microscopically; it is not an extra bedside test. The basal lamina is part of the epithelial attachment interface, whereas the basement membrane also includes connective support. Ground substance is the nonfibrous matrix around cells; a fibroblast actively makes matrix and a fibrocyte is a less active form. The tissue-healing figure shows a clot, inflammatory cleanup, new capillaries and fibroblast-rich repair followed by a contracting scar. Angiogenesis names new vessel growth, not infection. Histamine contributes to dilation and permeability, while clotting limits blood loss: these simultaneous responses do different jobs.
把指定组织术语表读成结构与功能图。组织学用显微方式研究组织结构，不是额外床边检查。基底板属于上皮附着界面的一部分，基底膜还包括结缔支持。基质中的无定形成分围绕细胞；成纤维细胞积极造基质，纤维细胞是较不活跃形态。组织愈合图串起血块、炎症清除、新毛细血管与富成纤维细胞的修复，继而瘢痕收缩。血管生成指新血管生长，不是感染。组胺参与扩张及通透增加，凝血限制失血；这些同时发生的反应承担不同工作。

00:28:37.680 --> 00:29:28.776
For the assigned cancer pages, separate a DNA-sequence mutation from an epigenetic change in how genetic information is used. Neither term means every altered cell has become cancer. Changes affecting growth control can accumulate; invasive malignant cells can cross tissue boundaries and may later establish distant disease. The source figure depicts disordered growth breaching the supporting layer, not proof that every tumor has already metastasized. New vessels may support either ordinary repair or tumor growth, depending on context. Surgery, radiation, cytotoxic medicines and selected molecular treatments act through different mechanisms and can affect healthy tissue too. This reading explains biology; it does not select a treatment for a particular patient.
指定癌症页须区分DNA序列突变，以及改变遗传信息使用方式的表观遗传变化。二者都不表示每个改变的细胞已成癌。影响生长控制的变化可累积；浸润性恶性细胞能跨组织边界，之后可能在远处建立病灶。来源图画的是异常生长突破支持层，不证明每个肿瘤已转移。新血管可支持普通修复或肿瘤，须看背景。手术、放疗、细胞毒药及特定分子治疗机制不同，也可能影响健康组织。此阅读解释生物学，不替某患者选择治疗。

00:29:28.776 --> 00:30:21.432
Decode the bone glossary without turning names into procedures. Osseous tissue means bone tissue; osteogenesis and ossification concern bone formation, with an ossification center marking a developing formation site. An osteoid scaffold is not yet fully mineralized bone. Articulation names a joint between skeletal elements; a nutrient foramen is an entry for supply, and central/Haversian versus perforating/Volkmann canals describe different routes inside bone. A lacuna houses a bone cell; canaliculi connect its processes to the surrounding network. An orthopedist specializes in musculoskeletal care. These distinctions explain why fracture can disrupt structure and supply, while open reduction still means surgical exposure rather than an open skin wound.
读骨术语，不能把名称变成操作。Osseous tissue即骨组织；osteogenesis及ossification讲成骨，骨化中心是发育中的形成区域；类骨质支架尚未充分矿化。Articulation指骨骼构件之间的关节，营养孔是供给入口，中央管或Havers管与穿通管或Volkmann管描述骨内不同通路。骨陷窝容纳骨细胞，骨小管把其突起接到周围网络。Orthopedist是骨骼肌肉专科医生。这些区别解释骨折为何破坏结构及供给；切开复位仍指手术暴露，不能当作皮肤开放伤。

00:30:21.432 --> 00:31:14.376
Connect the final muscle terms to adaptation rather than memorizing similar prefixes. Hypertrophy increases the size of existing fibers; hyperplasia means an increase in cell number, not a synonym for one observed cell division or for ordinary skeletal training enlargement. Atrophy loses size and functional reserve. ATPase activity breaks down ATP, and phosphocreatine transfers phosphate to help restore ATP rapidly; neither creates energy from nothing. Myoglobin holds oxygen inside muscle, while angiogenesis can expand the capillary supply during adaptation. These changes support sustained metabolism but do not make active muscle independent of circulation. A trapped, ischemic muscle therefore cannot be judged safe simply because it once had good endurance.
把末页肌肉术语连到适应，不能只背相似词头。肥大是已有肌纤维变大，增生是细胞数增加，不等于观察到一次分裂，也不是普通骨骼肌训练增大的同义词。萎缩丧失大小及功能储备。ATP酶活性分解ATP，磷酸肌酸转移磷酸帮助快速恢复ATP，二者都不凭空造能量。肌红蛋白在肌内储氧，适应中的血管生成可扩大毛细供给。这些变化支持持续代谢，却不能让工作肌肉不依赖循环。因此受困缺血肌肉不能因以前耐力好，就被判安全。

00:31:14.376 --> 00:32:10.416
Read the twitch graph before using its vocabulary. A stimulus is followed by a latent interval while excitation and calcium coupling develop, then rising mechanical tension and finally relaxation. No detectable tension yet does not mean no electrical or cellular activity. The tension-time trace, the recording apparatus and a membrane action potential are distinct things; do not use the glossary instrument shorthand to confuse them. Recruitment and firing frequency grade whole-muscle force. An isometric hold can generate force without visible movement; controlled eccentric lowering generates force while the active muscle lengthens. For an original example, compare lifting a light bag, lowering it slowly and holding it still: shortening, active lengthening and near-constant length do not mean on, off and off.
先读单收缩图，再使用术语。刺激后有潜伏间隔，期间兴奋与钙耦联发展；随后机械张力上升，最终舒张。尚无可测张力，不等于没有电活动或细胞活动。张力随时间曲线、记录仪器及膜动作电位是不同事物，不能被术语表的仪器简写混在一起。募集及发放频率使整肌力量分级。等长保持可在无可见动作时产力；有控制地离心放下时，活动肌延长仍产力。原创例：比较举轻包、慢慢放下、静止拿住，分别为缩短、主动延长、长度近恒定，不能解释成开、关、关。

00:32:10.416 --> 00:32:20.184
You should now be able to explain why catastrophic hemorrhage is treated immediately in this scenario and how the crew continues airway and breathing support in parallel.
你现在应能解释本情景为何立即处理灾难性出血，以及团队如何并行继续气道及呼吸支持。

00:32:20.184 --> 00:32:31.464
Choose the appropriate bleeding-control method, demonstrate correct CAT and binder landmarks in supervised practice, and distinguish the school timer from actual clinical success.
应能选择适当止血方法，在监督训练中展示正确CAT及骨盆带定位，并区分学校计时与真实临床成功。

00:32:31.464 --> 00:32:43.872
Recognize that concealed bleeding, crush physiology and a new chest problem may coexist. Reassessment must test your first explanation rather than merely repeat the first treatment.
应认识到隐匿失血、挤压生理及新胸部问题可以并存。复评应检验最初解释，而不是单纯重复首次治疗。

00:32:43.872 --> 00:32:54.168
Use the paired Nancy reading and school-linked trauma reading to compare mechanisms, research claims and current local guidance, then rehearse the original checks and MIST.
可用中英对照Nancy阅读及学校创伤链接阅读，对照机制、研究主张与当地现行指南，再演练原创自查及MIST。
